From 61e400b0f45841958acc429e0965564c1d8f97e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Suresh, Prashanth" <prashanth.suresh@intel.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 07:17:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media-driver: Add missing i915/include dir for generic
 mos_bufmgr.h

A real flashfiles build failed with a fatal file-not-found error:
media_common/linux/common/os/mos_os_specific.h unconditionally
includes "mos_bufmgr.h" (the generic MOS_BUFMGR type used regardless
of which KMD backend -- i915 or xe -- is active at runtime), but its
containing directory, media_softlet/linux/common/os/i915/include, was
never added to local_include_dirs. Only its uapi/ subdirectory was.

This directory was previously assumed to be legacy-i915-only and
therefore excluded from the Android.bp include-dirs sweep, but the
header it provides is load-bearing for the generic (non-backend-
specific) media_common code, not just the i915 backend itself.
Confirmed collision-free against i915_production/include and
xe/include (no shared header filenames).

Tracked-On: NIACP3-1547
Signed-off-by: Suresh, Prashanth <prashanth.suresh@intel.com>
---
 Android.bp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/Android.bp b/Android.bp
index 00049e070..05d96ae9e 100644
--- a/Android.bp
+++ b/Android.bp
@@ -2754,6 +2754,7 @@ cc_library_shared {
         "media_softlet/linux/common/cp/ddi",
         "media_softlet/linux/common/ddi",
         "media_softlet/linux/common/os",
+        "media_softlet/linux/common/os/i915/include",
         "media_softlet/linux/common/os/i915/include/uapi",
         "media_softlet/linux/common/os/i915_production/include",
         "media_softlet/linux/common/os/levelzero",
-- 
2.34.1

